# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Copied into build/web by `flutter build`.
#
# Everything revalidates. Flutter's main files are not named by content hash,
# so a long cache would keep a seller on an old build after a deploy — the
# "new version, reload" bar would appear and reloading would load the old one
# again. `no-cache` still lets the browser keep the file; it only asks whether
# it changed, which is a 304 when it has not.
# ponytail: one rule for every file, so canvaskit and fonts revalidate too.
# Give them their own long max-age if first-load time on a repeat visit matters.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
